   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">-	MoU with the Government signed on Digital Transformation
-	Network of Digital ambassadors created
-	National consultative/advisory mechanism on Digital transformation institutionalized under the Government
-	National integrated digital strategy and roadmap developed
-	Digital readiness assessment report developed
-	Number of Innovation challenges launched
-	Number of public services digitalized
-	Number of private companies supported in development of innovational projects (including % of women led businesses)
-	Number of digital labs equipped with ITC equipment
-	Number of thematic events organized</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">-	No collaboration framework with the Government on Digital Transformation
-	No discussions platforms in place with Government and other stakeholders on Digital transformation
-	No Digital Transformation vision, strategy and roadmap of the Country
-	Limited understanding of the resources needed to be mobilized for Digital transformation roadmap 
-	No initiatives of involvement of private sector in digital transformation of public services
-	No initiative for stimulating private sector to develop innovational projects related digital transformation of real economic sector
-	Very low % of digital inclusion and literacy</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">To Support digital transformation of the Government
1. Government-private sector dialog. Build a platform for a dialogue between government and private sector on digital transformation of Moldova with elaboration of the Vision and Strategy on digital transformation. 
2. Digitalization of the public services and solutions for citizens and the local private sector. Launch the digital innovation challenges with thematic focus on digital transformation.
3. Digital Literacy. Technology/solutions transfer, adaptation and scaling-up to improve the Digital Literacy in the country.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Government-private sector dialog
  - A Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between UNDP Moldova and Government signed;
  - A Digital Readiness Assessment (DRA) launched in partnership with the Government of Moldova and with both UNDP Digital Office in New York and the Global Centre for 
   Technology, Innovation and Sustainable Development from Singapore;
  - Based on the Digital Readiness Assessment findings and in partnership with the International Telecommunication Unit, a Digital transformation Compact for Moldova 
   (Compact) was developed;
  - A national network of Media Digital Ambassadors &#x2013; 14 journalists from all regions of Moldova was created;
  - A strategic team to provide necessary technical assistance to the Government in developing the next Digital Transformation Strategy for Moldova was established;
  - Development of the National Digital Transformation Strategy for 2022-2030 was initiated;

2. Digitalization of the public services and solutions for citizens and the local private sector
  - 2 digital innovation challenges were organized, and 6 small ICT companies supported to test innovative solutions;

3. Digital Literacy
  - 19 schools across the country were equipped with modern technologies in partnership with &#x201c;Tekwill in Every School&#x201d; network;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">To Support digital transformation of the Government
1. Government-private sector dialog. Build a platform for a dialogue between government and private sector on digital transformation of Moldova with elaboration of the Vision and Strategy on digital transformation. 
2. Digitalization of the public services and solutions for citizens and the local private sector. Launch the digital innovation challenges with thematic focus on digital transformation.
3. Digital Literacy. Technology/solutions transfer, adaptation and scaling-up to improve the Digital Literacy in the country.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Government-private sector dialog
&#x2022;	 With the help of the Project the Government established the platform for a dialogue with private sector and international partners on digital transformation of Moldova. 
&#x2022;	The Project is providing targeted assistance on digital transformation for the key Ministries and Agencies of Moldova:
o	Prime Minister and State Chancellery &#x2013; establishment of the Intelligence Unit;
o	Ministry of Foreign Affairs and European Integration &#x2013; Institution digital readiness assessment;
o	Ministry of Internal Affairs &#x2013; Institution digital readiness assessment and assistance to respond to the refugees crisis from Ukraine;
o	Ministry of Labor and Ministry of Infrastructure &#x2013; targeted assistance to respond to the energy crisis, including creation of the digital platform for the Energy Vulnerability Fund;
o	Ministry of Agriculture &#x2013; initiating a feasibility study on creation of National Farm Registry, etc.
&#x2022;	The Project, in collaboration with Digital Office from NY, initiated with the Government an activity focused on modernization of the integrated national data ecosystem governance stream that will become the next stage of the digital transformation of Moldova;
&#x2022;	Development of the National Digital Transformation Strategy for 2022-2030 was significantly advanced. The draft Strategy developed and the Government is working on launching the National consultation stage.

2. Digitalization of the public services and solutions for citizens and the local private sector
Six digital innovation challenges launched by the project to accelerate engagement of the vibrant ICT private sector to digital transformation of Moldova. Selected applicants are working on digital solutions in the following areas: creation of a drone assistance network for farmers, creation of an electronic bills system for companies, creation of a credit providing mechanism for start-ups and creation of QR billing for public services for citizens, Digital Mobile Signature/ Mobile Identity (MobiSign) solution, Digital Wallet (MWallet) solution, digital solutions for SME sector, etc. One innovation challenge launched in collaboration with Digital Office from NY that is focused on promotion of Digital Public Goods platforms is at the stage of evaluation of participants in the challenge.

3. Digital Literacy
The project further concentrated on development of the National network of Agents of Change to promote the digital literacy of the country. This includes creation of DigiLabs in schools, creation of Digital Media Ambassadors National group, building the capacity of libraries to provide targeted digital assistance to citizens, etc. 

Digi Labs network implementation through the Tekwill in every school network increased to 35 schools (20 schools supported by UNDP (out of which, 10 schools are supported in partnership with RoAID) from different parts of the country. Additionally, the project, under the Tekwill in Every School initiative, developed a concept of a Moldovan Digital School and its core elements: interactive content; digital pedagogy, digital and pedagogy transformation strategy, innovative learning spaces, performant equipment, 21st century skills assessment model, STEAM-based learning projects. 25 schools from Moldova have been selected to benefit from the Digital School initiative, participate in a unique pilot and develop an individual pedagogy and digital transformation school strategy. 150 teachers are involved already in this process.

Moreover, more than 2000 librarians (Ministry of Culture) and social assistants (Ministry of Labor) are prepared by the project to help the citizens to digitally register on Energy Vulnerability platform to receive the compensations from the Government, indirectly contributing to the improvement of the digital literacy throughout the entire country. More than 800,000 households registered which made the platform one of the most used one in the country.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
